course: dictionary
lesson: 2184
title: Cosmic: space, size and slang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cosmic is linked to cosmos, another word for the universe. Its first meaning is about space: things that are from or belong to the universe beyond the Earth. «Cosmic rays» and «cosmic dust» come from space, not from our planet.
explain: Writers often stretch a word past its first meaning. «A black hole is not a hole and not a cosmic vacuum cleaner» compares a black hole to a machine that sucks everything in. Here cosmic means very great and powerful, like something from the universe.
explain: Use the clues around the word to choose the right meaning. If the sentence is about planets, stars or space, it means from space. If it is about something huge, like «a disaster of cosmic proportions», it means very great. If someone says «That's cosmic, man» in a dreamy, old-fashioned way, it means amazing.
fact: Cosmic is linked to cosmos, which means the universe.
fact: «Cosmic rays» are high-energy particles that travel to Earth from space.
fact: «Cosmic dust» is tiny bits of matter floating in space.
fact: «Cosmic» can mean very great in size or importance, as in «a disaster of cosmic proportions».
fact: «A cosmic joke» means fate playing a trick on someone, and «That's cosmic» is informal slang for amazing.
exercise: «Cosmic rays» and «cosmic dust» come from where? | The bottom of the sea | A school science lab | *Outer space | Inside a volcano
exercise: «A disaster of cosmic proportions» means a disaster that is how big? | *Very great in size or importance | Very small and quiet | Only the size of a kitchen | Cold and wet
exercise: Ben says, «That's cosmic, man!» in a dreamy voice. What does cosmic mean here? | Boring | Lost | *Amazing | Dirty
test: In «a black hole is not a hole and not a cosmic vacuum cleaner», what does cosmic mean? | Short and rude | Very great and powerful, like something from the universe | Very wet and grey | *Hungry
test: Which phrase means fate playing a trick on someone? | *A cosmic joke | A cosmic bath | A cosmic cookie | A cosmic nap
exam: Which thing is a «cosmic ray»? | *A stream of high-energy particles from space | A bright laser pointer in class | A fish with spots | A ray of sunshine on a beach
